# Line endings for the files that actually care.
#
# core.autocrlf=true (this repo's default on Windows) would otherwise hand the
# POSIX launcher CRLF endings, and `#!/usr/bin/env sh\r` is not a shebang on
# macOS or Linux -- it is "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
auto      text eol=lf
auto.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.sh      text eol=lf

# The vendored tars tree is a VERBATIM copy of somebody else's code, and a
# licence obligation is easier to honour when the bytes on a fresh clone
# are the bytes that were copied. Without this, git normalises LF to CRLF
# on checkout and every file in vendor/ differs from upstream in every
# line -- which makes 'copied verbatim' a claim a diff would contradict.
autoforge/vendor/** -text
